[h2]Sector Control[/h2]
Three sides (BLUFOR, OPFOR and Independent) capture and hold sectors to score points. Holding more sectors raises the scoring rate. The first side to 100 points wins. You can return through eligible captured sectors, groupmates and mobile respawn vehicles. Up to 150 players, with AI filling the open slots.

[h2]On the battlefield[/h2]
[list]
[*]Use the group menu ([b]U[/b]) to organize players and AI. AI groups attack and defend objectives, deliver mobile respawn vehicles to the front and can use transport, ground vehicles and boats where available.
[*]Stabilize and revive downed teammates. You can also move injured teammates out of danger.
[*]Order eligible vehicles, use service points and harbors, and collect supply drops. Vehicle choices depend on the terrain and your rank.
[*]The HUD shows sector ownership, ticket rates and respawn information. Press [b]F2[/b] to toggle the HUD and [b]F4[/b] for settings.
[*]Information boards at the base explain the rules and show the equipment list and your statistics.
[*]At the end of a round, an end screen shows the winner, MVPs and the leaderboard, and players vote for the next layout.
[/list]

[h2]Rank and perks[/h2]
Earn XP for capturing and contesting sectors, revives, eliminations, assists and kill-streak bounties, and for transporting teammates, defending sectors and repairing vehicles. Ranks open new weapons, gear and vehicles. Use the Arsenal to build and save loadouts from the equipment you have unlocked.
[list]
[*]Rank 1: Experience and Medic.
[*]Ranks 5, 7 and 10: Stamina, Marksman and Machinegunner.
[*]Ranks 15, 18 and 20: Launcher, Armor and Grenadier.
[*]Ranks 22 and 25: Explosives and Suppressor.
[/list]
Perk slots unlock at ranks 1, 6, 18, 35, 67 and 100.

[h2]Lobby parameters[/h2]
Choose the layout or let the game pick one. Random layouts can use a set size or scale with player count. The host can set vehicle spawn rules and cooldown, sector messages, thermal vision, launcher and high-caliber damage, progression storage, third-person view, weather, start time, night skip and time multipliers.

The mission includes Killfeed, Dynamic Weather, 3D Icons, Map Marker, Earplugs, Jump, Holster, Unflip, Magazine Repack and Disable Tactical View. Stamina uses the mission's own system: the HUD bar limits sprinting, and when it runs low you walk and your aim sways more.

[h2]Start the scenario[/h2]
Host the scenario in multiplayer and open Parameters in the lobby. The Tanoa edition requires the Apex expansion. The Chernarus 2020 edition requires the CUP addons listed on that Workshop page.

